## In-app chats no longer force the scroll position

Context:
Graph Chat (Digital Twin) and the Ontology Studio floating assistant pinned
the messages pane to the bottom (`scrollTop = scrollHeight`) on every
rendered element: each streamed step update, the streaming bubble, the final
reply, tool traces, pending-action cards, errors, the resource advisory, the
thinking indicator, every restored-history message and answers pushed from
Analytics "interpret". A user who scrolled up to read an earlier answer was
pulled back down on each update. The only programmatic scroll left is the
natural one: when the user sends a message, their own message is brought
into view once. No "jump to latest" button existed, so none was added.

Changes:
1. src/front/static/query/js/query-chat.js
   - Removed the forced scroll from `appendMessage`, `appendError`,
     `appendResourceAdvisory`, `createStreamingBubble`,
     `updateStreamingBubble` and `finalizeStreamingBubble`. History restore,
     confirm-action results and `appendChatAssistantMessage` therefore no
     longer move the pane either.
   - New `revealSentMessage()`, called once from `sendMessage` right after
     the user's message is appended (before the streaming bubble).
   - Deleted `showThinking` / `hideThinking`: already unused (the streaming
     bubble replaced them) and they carried a forced scroll.
2. src/front/static/query/css/query-chat.css
   - Removed the `.graph-chat-messages .assistant-thinking` rule that only
     the deleted `showThinking` used; the thinking-dots rules stay (the
     streaming bubble uses them).
3. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-assistant.js
   - Removed the forced scroll from `appendMessage`, `appendError` and
     `showThinking`.
   - New `revealSentMessage()`, called once from `sendMessage` right after
     the user's message is appended.
4. tests/units/front/test_chat_no_forced_scroll.py (new)
   - Node harness runs both modules against a stubbed DOM whose messages
     pane records every `scrollTop` write. Graph Chat: a streamed run (tool
     steps, final reply with tool trace, pending action and resource
     advisory), HTTP error, network error, history restore and an Analytics
     push. Ontology assistant: reply, server error, network error. Sending
     writes `scrollTop` exactly once, before the response, and a reader who
     scrolled up during the response stays where they are.
   - Static guard: neither chat module has `scrollTop =`, `scrollIntoView`,
     `scrollTo(` or `scrollBy(` outside `revealSentMessage`, and the helper
     is called only from `sendMessage`.

Notes:
- Restored history now opens at the top of the pane (oldest message first)
  instead of jumping to the newest one.
- Out of scope (not AI chats): the comments offcanvas and the review-history
  modal still scroll to the newest comment when they render, and task
  activity logs (task overlay, SHACL facets, Data Quality, settings logs)
  still follow the latest log line.

Modified files:
- src/front/static/query/js/query-chat.js
- src/front/static/query/css/query-chat.css
- src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-assistant.js
- tests/units/front/test_chat_no_forced_scroll.py
- changelogs/v0.9.1/simyung-yang_2026-11-04.log

